@ref Article 3.1 (src 132-154); Article 1 (src 30-32)
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `A death claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 3.1 — the death benefit on` `the claim` MEANS
          `the claim`'s `the schedule`'s `sum assured`                      -- i)
    PLUS  `the surrender value on` `the valuation after the claim date`     -- ii)
    PLUS  `the claim`'s `amounts deducted from the death to the notice`     -- iii)
    PLUS  `the claim`'s `rider benefits payable`                            -- iv)
    MINUS `the valuation after the claim date`'s `premium debt`             -- v)
    WHERE
        `the valuation after the claim date` MEANS
            `the valuation on the next Valuation Date after` (`the claim`'s `date the Company received the complete and valid claim`) `among` (`the claim`'s `valuations after the death`)

§§ `3.2 Exclusions from the death benefit`

-- If the death results directly or indirectly from (i) committing, or intentionally
-- committing, a criminal offence, or (ii) any death related to AIDS, ARC or HIV infection,
-- the Company does not pay 3.1 and pays instead the surrender value on the next Valuation
-- Date after the claim date, less the premium debt (which, as in 3.1, is then deducted
-- twice).
--
-- WHOSE OFFENCE. Limb (i) has no subject. Read as the Life Insured's own offence: the
-- literal reading, any person's offence, excludes the victim of a murder (NOTES.md fork
-- register and findings; Article 24 of the Law reads an unclear term for the buyer).
-- Limb (ii) has no waiting period and no exception (a transfusion, say).
-- src:110 | 3.2
